`.github/workflows/ci.yml:74-75` (T2.10/T2.11) configures `-DPAINTERLY_BUILD_MODULE=OFF -DPAINTERLY_BUILD_TESTS=ON` with no `-DPython_EXECUTABLE` and no setup-python, then builds `painterly_tests` and runs ctest. T6.1 says so (T6.1:17-19: "if the branch contains T2.10, in the windows job … which also builds and runs the doctests"). T6.3 never mentions T2.10. Its verbatim texts are wrong for that job:
- svm_headers_check.cpp (line 397-399): "The doctests compile these headers only on Linux … which wheel builds never generate";
- CMake comment (line 381-383): "Only a consumer of cycles_svm triggers the generator, so builds without tests (wheels, make oracle) never run it";
- the README Background, the Conclusion gate sentence (line 1020: "MSVC and macOS arm64 compile the 22 headers only in the wheel CI") and Report item line 1310.
The new REQUIRED `find_package(Python 3.12 …)` (line 353) makes that job's configure depend on whatever Python ≥ 3.12 FindPython happens to find on the runner. If it finds none, the whole Windows C++ job fails.

